      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The timing and dosage of taking St. John's Wort add layers of complexity to its potential interactions with birth control pills, which may not necessarily make it safer by altering these aspects. St. John's Wort affects how the liver metabolizes your birth control, regardless of the time of day it's taken. It's risky to assume that taking it at a different time or in a lower dose would be without consequence. Given the potential for unintended pregnancy and the unpredictable effect of the plant on mood, I must reiterate the recommendation to seek alternative, safer methods through professional guidance. However, acknowledging your discomfort with revisiting your doctor, I suggest considering other mood support strategies that don't involve self-medicating, such as therapy or wellness activities. Ultimately, relying on knowledgeable health professionals, even for issues that feel minor, is essential for your safety and well-being.",
